            <ArticleTitle>Nurses struggle to help pupils with long-term conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most school nurses are not confident they can give essential support to pupils with long-term health conditions. Research by the National Children's Bureau found that, due to heavy workloads and the need to work across several schools, nine out of ten school nurses were less confident they can help children with conditions such as diabetes and asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
